# New Demo
- Rewritten using Sigma.js + Graphololgy instead of React Flow

# Features
- MUCH improved performance. Can handle exponentially more nodes and edges
- Has "Add Node", "Delete Node", and "Clear All Nodes" buttons that work roughly the same as the old demo
- Has the same click-to-add edges as before
- Slightly improved visuals/colors
- Improved "Add Hopfield Network" button. Works the same as the "Add Node" button but with a Hopfield Network of n nodes

# What's Needed
- Saving as a photo
- Saving / loading presets (I messed with this a bit and kinda got it working but not well enough to keep. It'd just replace the whole current graph instead of adding to it. I (Ryan) can work on this more later)
- Grid implementation (I struggled with this for a while and couldn't get it working, but the same thing happened last time and Shaun got it working quickly, so)l
- Learning / Simulation / Visualization phases
- Bug fixes below (most importantly the weird camera and node-placing behavior)

# Current Issues
- Double-click zoom-in sucks and should be disabled
- Camera is being super weird and tries to fit itself to nodes when effectively anything happens
- Nodes try to orient themselves or "balance" themseles out when being placed instead of staying locked in place or going where they should
- Adding a hopfield network compresses everything else. I think this has to do withthe same "balancing" in the previous bullet